import csv
D='/home/user/unbound/requirements/reconciliation/2026-11-23/data'
WHO="Integrating agent under owner delegation (instruction 2026-11-23: 'make best decisions and note')"
X={
"RCD-001":("Adopt all refinement records and gap requirements into the domain files, with originals annotated as refined or superseded and kept verbatim. Records that depend on a legal decision are adopted with status 'adopted-provisional (counsel validation pending)'.","Owner instructed adoption; keeping originals verbatim preserves history","none","Owner reverses any adoption"),
"RCD-002":("Owner waiver recorded for requirements-only work. The Conditor bootstrap (AGENT-MISSION step 0) remains mandatory before any implementation scaffold or EF component installation.","Requirements work does not install components; implementation does","Owner confirmation of waiver wording","Start of implementation"),
"RCD-003":("'Unbound' remains the platform's internal name; 'Strata' refers only to the Echelon schema tool. UNB-EXP-002 is superseded: public identity is the sponsor's white-label brand plus a mandatory legal-sponsor disclosure and a protected legal-term list.","Avoids a name collision with an EF component and resolves the white-label contradiction","Owner may rename the platform; if so, choose a name other than Strata","Owner naming decision"),
"RCD-004":("Tenant = legal sponsor. One database per legal sponsor on shared managed PostgreSQL, deployed from one release. Distribution partners get separate schemas inside their sponsor's database. Dedicated cells only on a cited contractual clause. Schema-per-tenant across sponsors and row-level security as a default are both rejected. Global hold watermark adopted.","Keeps each sponsor's books transactional, isolates legal entities physically, and respects the existing owner position against default row-level isolation","Architecture spike DG-09 and DG-11","A contract requires dedicated infrastructure"),
"RCD-005":("Build the deterministic approval tier. Until counsel and the sponsor board approve delegation, its outcome is 'ApproveRecommended', which a human approves in one-click batches (A4). After approval the same rule outcome becomes the A3 approval itself, with no code change, only an authority-flag change.","Builds the efficient path without assuming the legal answer","Counsel Q1 + sponsor board resolution","Counsel opinion received"),
"RCD-006":("Adopt RR-REQ-X-007-r1. An IRS-status check happens at approval and again at payment release, using an observation retrieved within the last 24 hours from the latest published TEOS/BMF/auto-revocation revision, with a per-sponsor snapshot. Deep review defaults to every 180 days (sponsor may tighten, not loosen), with automatic refresh starting 30 days before expiry. Cross-sponsor evidence may be reused as input only.","Rev. Proc. 2018-32 reliance is per grant date; the 24-hour window bounds staleness without real-time dependence","Counsel Q2","IRS changes publication cadence; counsel opinion"),
"RCD-007":("Adopt the authority-keyed retention catalog: 7-year platform floor (policy); OFAC records 10 years; basis and carryover records 7 years after final disposition; reliance snapshots at least the floor. Disposition runs as approved class-level batches; no automatic deletion.","Executable precedence with the least human work","Counsel Q5","Counsel retention schedule"),
"RCD-008":("Defer the visual email designer and IVR. Release 1 uses governed per-event templates with typed tokens and locked legal clauses, plus numeric record references printed on documents.","No demand evidence; Forma email designer is unbuilt","none","Two or more sponsors require it contractually"),
"RCD-009":("Folio print components provide document markup. Unbound runs a server-side headless-Chromium render to produce deterministic PDFs (Folio tier P2, to be proven by spike). Every document also has an accessible HTML rendition generated from the same snapshot, which satisfies WCAG. Tagged PDF/UA is a later enhancement. No Typst at release 1. The document registry hashes the PDF and the source snapshot independently of the renderer.","Stays within EF components; accessibility met through the HTML twin; avoids a new runtime dependency","DG-04 spike: byte-identical re-render and throughput","Spike fails determinism"),
"RCD-010":("Defer conversion to the Praxis requirement catalog until the UI requirements are further refined (owner instruction 2026-11-23).","Owner instruction","none","Owner says convert"),
"RCD-011":("Confirmed exclusions for release 1: native mobile apps, payroll round-ups, direct crypto custody (accept only via a liquidating intermediary), international grants, donor-level impact measurement, visual email designer, IVR.","Evidence in report 05","none","Market evidence changes"),
"RCD-012":("No separate protective emergency plane. Use managed-database high availability plus a read-only degraded mode in which payment release fails closed. Holds published before an outage remain binding after it.","No failure mode shown that managed HA plus degraded mode cannot handle","none","An incident analysis shows such a failure mode"),
"RCD-013":("Release 1 covers: cash (ACH, wire, check) and publicly traded securities contributions; complex assets only through a partner intermediary that delivers cash; standard DAF only; domestic grants to excepted public charities (509(a)(1)/(2), certified Type I/II/FI-III supporting organizations, government units) by ACH and check; one custodian and one partner payment rail; sponsor fee schedules; statements and acknowledgments; donor/advisor/successor, sponsor-operations, charity and embedded-status experiences; one tenancy profile. Out: sponsor ERP, GRC product, international, ER grants, workplace and campaign products, AI agents acting on accounts.","Smallest coherent, commercially viable slice","none","Owner changes scope"),
"RCD-014":("Release 1 permits grants only to excepted recipients (see RCD-013), with a donor-control certification for supporting organizations and the related-party payee block always on. Expenditure-responsibility, private-foundation, non-functionally-integrated Type III, foreign and individual recipients are rejected with an explanation.","Avoids every §4966 class that needs ER until counsel answers","Counsel Q3, Q4","Counsel opinion; product demand for ER grants"),
"RCD-015":("Adopt UNB-RCN-GRT-006/007 and UNB-RCN-REG-003. Screen donors, advisors, successors, recipient entities, payee account holders and the recipient's officers where data is available, at onboarding, at grant approval, at payment release and on every list update. Potential matches are held; humans disposition them; a confirmed match leads to Blocked and OFAC reporting.","Statutory prohibition with strict liability","Counsel review of ScreeningScope matrix","OFAC guidance change"),
"RCD-016":("Pledge handling is sponsor policy. Platform default is 'NoticeConditions' (grants that satisfy Notice 2017-73 are allowed; the sponsor never references the pledge; remittance metadata strips pledge references). Sponsors may choose 'Prohibited'.","Matches IRS reliance guidance and market variation","Counsel confirmation that Notice 2017-73 remains reliance guidance","IRS final guidance"),
"RCD-017":("Reservation against capacity computed in the same transaction. Grant states Reserved → FundingPlanned → Funded before payment. Each pool keeps a cash liquidity buffer (sponsor-set percentage, default 2% of pool value) so routine grants fund from cash without per-grant trades. Percentage grants fix their amount at approval.","Prevents overcommitment and keeps funding deterministic","CFO/investment committee confirms buffer default","Buffer breaches repeat"),
"RCD-018":("Fee base is end-of-day fund market value, including reserved but unpaid amounts and excluding fees embedded in pool NAV. Fees accrue daily (actual/365) and settle monthly, with no fee on accrued fees. Minimum fees apply per sponsor schedule. Fees are recognized as sponsor revenue when settled.","Testable and industry-consistent","Sponsor CFO","Sponsor contract terms"),
"RCD-019":("Contributions credit grantable capacity only on Final: ACH after the sponsor-set return window (default 5 business days); wire on receipt; check on clear; securities on settlement into custody. Acknowledgment is issued on CompletedGiftDetermined ∧ SponsorAccepted. Accepted assets never return to a donor; returned grant funds go back to the originating fund.","Statutory acknowledgment rules and §4966","CPA on completed-gift rule table","Counsel or CPA opinion"),
"RCD-020":("Continuous automated reconciliation. Routine matched items auto-pass. Independent sampled attestation of at least 5% of passes per month. Any unexplained cash break blocks statement publication for the affected funds. Security price breaks follow the sponsor tolerance. Allocation method is declared per custody account. Fund and restriction are balancing segments.","Automation with control","Controller","Audit finding"),
"RCD-021":("Release 1 does not pay advisors with a personal relationship to the donor from DAF assets. Investment managers engaged by the sponsor under sponsor contract are allowed. Watch item on REG-142338-07.","Conservative pending §4958 and proposed-regulation analysis","Counsel Q-advisor (§4958)","Counsel opinion; final regulations"),
"RCD-022":("Adopt hold-on-notice, suspend-on-verified-death, then activate succession. OD-03: approved unpaid grants proceed unless sponsor policy says otherwise. Dormancy default: 36 months with no advisor activity, then 12 months of outreach on all verified channels and to successors, then a charitable default per the program terms (A4 approval). Closure and outbound transfer follow the state machines in UNB-RCN-ENT-005..007.","Removes indefinite limbo while honouring sponsor control","Sponsor operations owner; counsel on escheat of balances (Q11)","Sponsor policy"),
"RCD-023":("Identity proofing is required for advisory-privilege holders and successors; sanctions screening for all parties. No CIP/AML programme unless counsel says one applies. Source-of-funds review only for complex assets and for contributions over a sponsor-set threshold.","No mandate found for a nonprofit sponsor; operator does not hold funds (Q8)","Counsel Q8","Custody model changes"),
"RCD-024":("Release 1 offers only the standard DAF product. The classification register is required before any new product type goes live. The Schedule D package (UNB-RCN-ENT-012) is a release-1 requirement.","§6033(k)","Counsel on future product types","New product type"),
"RCD-025":("A0–A5 is the single authority scale. The other three scales are mapped onto it. AI field help is limited to surfaces with a published assistance contract.","One vocabulary","none","—"),
"RCD-026":("Adopt the exception-first experience model (report 10 and 16). Configurable dashboards are deferred. Desktop-first is allowed for finance and close; donor, advisor and approval journeys must be phone-complete.","Removes department queues","none","User research contradicts"),
"RCD-027":("Technology mandates are reworded 'adopted by ADR after verification'. For release 1 the decisions are: Forma (UI patterns), Folio (document markup), Limen (browser runtime) and Strata (schema governance), each subject to licence review for commercial use. Ledger and event store are Unbound-owned on managed PostgreSQL (RR-UNB-PLAT-007-r1).","Verified capabilities (report 13)","Counsel on EF licence terms (commercial-launch blocker, not a design blocker)","Licence review result"),
"RCD-028":("Use a partner payment rail for ACH (no own ACH origination) and bank positive-pay for checks. Adopt the Unknown-resolution protocol, check lifecycle, DestinationEvidence table and return-to-fund rules. Uncashed checks are voided after 180 days, re-credited to the fund, and the charity is contacted; escheat applicability goes to counsel per state.","Partner rails cut scope; check rules are sponsor policy","Counsel Q11; rail partner due diligence","Rail selection"),
"RCD-029":("Propagate holds and verified public-source facts to every affected sponsor; never propagate sponsor-private investigation content.","Safety plus confidentiality","Counsel on defamation-sensitive facts","—"),
"RCD-030":("No individualized tax advice. Donor summaries and assistant answers use counsel-approved disclosures, including that DAF contributions do not qualify for the nonitemizer deduction (IR-2026-135). Bunching calculators are excluded from release 1.","Conflict of interest and OBBBA","Counsel/CPA approve disclosure text","—"),
"RCD-031":("Design for SOC 1 Type II (fund-accounting controls) and SOC 2 Type II (platform security). Readiness only; no attestation claimed.","Institutional buyers rely on ICFR","Compliance owner","—"),
}
rows=list(csv.DictReader(open(f'{D}/decisions.csv')))
out=[dict(r,status="decided-provisional" if X[r['decision_id']][2]!="none" else "decided",decided_option=X[r['decision_id']][0],decision_basis=X[r['decision_id']][1],validation_required=X[r['decision_id']][2],revisit_trigger=X[r['decision_id']][3],decided_by=WHO,decided_on="2026-11-23") for r in rows]
with open(f'{D}/decisions.csv','w',newline='') as f:
    w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=list(out[0]),quoting=csv.QUOTE_ALL); w.writeheader(); w.writerows(out)
Q=[("Q1","Delegated deterministic approval; fund-manager identity","Human approves in one-click batches until counsel and board approve delegation (RCD-005)."),
("Q2","Cross-sponsor charity evidence; grant-date check","Per-sponsor reliance snapshot at approval and release; shared evidence is an input only (RCD-006)."),
("Q3","Supporting-organization control certification; Notice 2006-109","A certification is required before any grant to Type I/II/FI-III organizations; no grant without one (UNB-RCN-REG-002)."),
("Q4","ED vs ER for foreign grants","Foreign grants excluded from release 1 (RCD-014)."),
("Q5","Retention schedule","Authority-keyed catalog with 7-year floor and 10-year OFAC class (RCD-007)."),
("Q6","OBBBA carryovers in bunching calculators","Bunching calculators excluded from release 1 (RCD-030)."),
("Q7","QCD to single-charity fund","QCDs are not accepted into DAFs; single-charity funds are out of release 1."),
("Q8","Money transmitter / GLBA / UPMIFA / ICA for operator","The operator never holds or moves funds: accounts are in the sponsor's name at its bank and custodian, and payments go through a partner rail under the sponsor's agreement. Pools are managed under the sponsor's investment policy, prudence standard applied as policy."),
("Q9","Revenue share and §4958 / Schedule L","Operator fees are a flat or tiered contract price not tied to a share of fund fees beyond disclosed schedules; no operator staff on sponsor boards; related-party disclosure in the sponsor contract."),
("Q10","E-SIGN consent for electronic acknowledgments","Obtain E-SIGN §7001(c) consent at onboarding; paper fallback on withdrawal of consent."),
("Q11","Escheat of uncashed checks","Void after 180 days, re-credit the fund, contact the charity, re-grant only on donor recommendation; counsel to confirm per state.")]
with open(f'{D}/counsel-positions.csv','w',newline='') as f:
    w=csv.writer(f,quoting=csv.QUOTE_ALL); w.writerow(("question_id","topic","provisional_position","status","decided_by","decided_on"))
    w.writerows((q,t,p,"provisional — counsel validation required before production",WHO,"2026-11-23") for q,t,p in Q)
print(len(out),len(Q))
